      {"when":"A game, or an app whose taps, answers, wins or other moments would feel better with sound (a quiz's right and wrong answers, a button that does something, a level clear), and the app has no sound yet.","use":"The Groove Lab player (import * as groove from '/build/vendor/groove-lab/1.0.0/player.js'): await groove.unlock() inside the first tap, then groove.sfx('click' | 'coin' | 'jump' | 'hit' | 'correct' | 'wrong' | 'win' | 'lose' | 'levelup' ...) at those moments, with a mute toggle kept in Twinkle.privateDb. Offer music too: compose a soundtrack as a Groove Lab song spec in a project module (soundtrack/<name>.js with export default { ...spec }, played with groove.createSoundtrack(spec).play({ fadeIn: 1 }) after unlock), or play the creator's published Groove Lab song with groove.loadPublishedSong(entryId) and show its credit."}
